      "updated": 1789634677168,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "If we traverse a collection using for loop and try\nto modify the collection ( add() or remove() )\nthen java throws an exception called\nConcurrentModificationException .\n\nIn order to modify in loop collection we can use\nIterator . \n\nIterator has a method called remove() which will\nremove objects from collection without any\nexception .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "If we traverse a collection using for loop and try to modify the collection ( add() or remove() ) then java throws an exception called ConcurrentModificationException .\n\nIn order to modify in loop collection we can use Iterator . \n\nIterator has a method called remove() which will remove objects from collection without any exception .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
